## GRADING (binding; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta and words.** A third path, or a changed byte of `DEPLOY.md` outside line 203 or unequal to `643c389e`'s = Blocker (STOP: new word); a `!`, a trailing backslash, a second physical line in the check = Major; non-ASCII in an added line, a skip/only = Major; a real organisation, client or person in the test's text = Major; a ticket key in the squash or PR text = Minor (corrected in your files), in a head commit message or a test comment = Note (a test TITLE naming a key = Note); `localdomain` in squash text = Major; a person's name or secret = Blocker; **a false sentence in a commit message, the PR title or the squash text = Minor, Major if about what the line accepts or refuses.**
- **G-2 the line.** A cell the OLD line refuses and the NEW accepts = Blocker, STOP (security-shaped). A flip outside the two named families and the N1 list, or a whole real script or the complete script (+ one blank line) refused = Major. An engine disagreement or error on a cell = Major if it changes a verdict the property names, Minor otherwise (NUL shapes: Note). A false refusal of a shape a real `pg_restore` can write = Major; of a hand-made shape = Note.
- **G-3 rows and plants.** A new row red or flaky on the merge result (3 runs, shuffle) = Major; counts other than the claims = Major unless explained; lint, prettier, typecheck, build or unit rc non-zero = Major; a failed set at the head not equal to the twin's = Major; a removed or weakened assertion = Major; **q3 or q4 leaving every b778 row green = Major**; a plant of q1-q16 (except a proved-equivalent q8) leaving every row green = Major; a new row that cannot fail (D5 a) = Major; **any of the 50 mutants that differs on a frame cell and leaves all 54 rows green (other than the proved equivalents) = Major**; a survivor of your own new mutants: graded by R2-G (D9); **any survivor in the `mutant-accepts` direction = Major whatever else holds.**
- **G-4 sentences.** `DEPLOY.md` is unchanged since `643c389e`: no new sentence can be false. B1173-3 is CARRIED and does not decide this verdict. INCOMPLETE (`:259`, `:204`) = Note for the product owner; `:263` = Note (PCOMP-117, out).
- **G-5 CodeQL and overlap.** An open alert on the branch = Blocker, STOP; no scan, no CI run = Condition (Tuesday lands only after a clean scan on the PR head); overlap with another open PR on a shared path = Major. **Always Note:** the local-host commit identity; the PR number is not yet known.
- **G-6 verdict (round 3, the granted final).** Any Blocker, or any Major that is not carried (B1173-3) = **`NO GO (round 3, final)`: nothing ships, no landing files, `residue.md` and the findings with their cells are the deliverable, there is NO round 4, and any further work needs the product owner's word on a card.** Only Minor, Note and Conditions = `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS`; none above Note = `GO`. Add ` (conditional: hosted CI and CodeQL NOT RUN)` while D7 is not "scanned and clean". **Do not soften a Major to reach a GO because this is the last round, and do not harden a Minor to a NO GO because survivors exist: grade by the rules above and show the table.**

